{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787175671106770001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"itchy-arbored-peccary","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"a539b50639d53de92f46ce8d9f5ac98e1a2e1db237f56a5ad0a452b30f4b5b6a","event_uuid":"8e09556e-13df-4f3a-b9a5-21d93836378e","position":{"commit_sha":"36f73ed7714490834aa39831d05e95a93ad9d225","position":"1787173743355609001-8e09556e-13df-4f3a-b9a5-21d93836378e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"113aafafc5c53a31c8acbd75717bba93bbb30b0a593126d3d9d4d63ae15abe6a","event_uuid":"1bc54adc-e8c1-48fe-a4a9-c5eeafa52e46","position":{"commit_sha":"486fc23a03585948056d839e93877005b0c3b61f","position":"1787173761432336001-1bc54adc-e8c1-48fe-a4a9-c5eeafa52e46"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787173743355609001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1bc54adc-e8c1-48fe-a4a9-c5eeafa52e46","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3a52-2d79-320d-4fed"}],"description":"## Discovered from\n\nrebar-debug on bug `masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle` (3a52-2d79-320d-4fed), root cause RC-B. See\nthat ticket's \"Phase 1 EXIT\" comment for the full evidence trail.\n\n## Problem\n\nTwo independent gaps leave the snapshot store with no size-based reclaim at all.\n\n**1. The backstop does not exist.** `docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md:72-73` and\nthe janitor module's own contract docstring (`src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:13-15`) both state\nthat reclamation is driven by a free-space watermark \"backstopped by the incrementally-\nmaintained byte total\". `_gc_pass` (`janitor.py:303-345`) reads only `free`\n(`shutil.disk_usage`) and each entry's `mtime`. It never consults `_cache.byte_total`. The only\nreader is `startup_sweep` (`janitor.py:251`), and that is reconciliation, not eviction. There\nis no store-size cap knob in the config surface either (`docs/config.md:474-484`).\n\n**2. The dominant consumer is not byte-accounted.** `cache.acquire` calls\n`add_bytes(entry_size(dest))` at `src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py:203`, but `materialize_tickets`\n(`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:616-708`) bypasses `acquire` entirely and never calls\n`add_bytes`. The `tickets-<sha>` entries are ~620 MiB each and are the largest thing in the\nstore, so even if the backstop above were implemented it would under-count them to **zero**.\n\n(`_is_entry` at `janitor.py:110-122` does recognise `tickets-` entries as evictable, so GC\nwould remove them if a trigger ever fired — the gap is purely in the trigger and the\naccounting.)\n\n## Impact\n\nOn the review-bot host this contributed to `rebar-root-disk-pressure` breaching 85% and\nreaching 90% with nothing reclaiming: the free-space trigger is unreachable below 93.3% used on\nthat volume (tracked on 3a52), the 7-day cold-trim exceeds the container's lifetime, and the\nthird trigger the ADR promises is absent.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `_gc_pass` gains a byte-total-driven eviction trigger with a documented, configurable cap\n      (or ADR 0005 and the janitor docstring are corrected to remove the promise — but then the\n      store has only one working trigger, so the cap is the expected resolution).\n- [ ] `materialize_tickets` records its entries in the store's byte total, so the accounting\n      reflects the entries that actually dominate it.\n- [ ] A test observes the untracked bytes RED (a store whose real size far exceeds the reported\n      `byte_total`) and GREEN after the fix.\n- [ ] `docs/config.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` and `docs/env-vars.md` document the new\n      cap knob (a docs test pins these — `tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py`).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3907-0110-7688-43bd","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Snapshot janitor's ADR-promised byte-total backstop is unimplemented, and materialize_tickets never byte-accounts its entries","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8e09556e-13df-4f3a-b9a5-21d93836378e","1bc54adc-e8c1-48fe-a4a9-c5eeafa52e46"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787175671106770001,"uuid":"170c7107-071d-4dd0-b534-115071902c5e"}